emy-id "q-97354" :question/problem "Let $V={R}^{3}$ be the vector space equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $x=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ and $y$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2(k\\cdot (-3))+5\\cdot (-3\\cdot 2)+3\\cdot (4\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-6k-30+36 \\\\  & =6-6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x,y⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6-6k & =0 \\\\ 6k & =6 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97354/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "46ebecec-2507-5893-8529-69e7bbd61765"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97354"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140263/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d330537c-aaaf-59b8-8c4a-6fb16adf3eb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140263/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "3aedfa59-331f-5b35-b154-846f12ea70d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140263/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "a46a93a5-b2c7-5738-ab86-46da85f50f5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140263/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2e02c947-d75f-5244-ab5f-91bb20564642" :answer/type :