with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1) \\\\  & =(2)(k-7)+(1)(k)+(2)(k-3) \\\\  & =2k-14+k+2k-6 \\\\  & =5k-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5k-20 & =0 \\\\ 5k & =20 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140265/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a348cfec-2c8f-5302-a94a-43a6c9330c34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140265"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97361/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "69b702c4-fc17-56da-87b5-95928e09085c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97361/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "5a11b1ae-fada-5005-bd66-ff5c77d9a95c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97361/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "029a292e-c0c8-5769-a8df-b8750573e36c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97361/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6b30ded1-ec87-5f36-b1fa-c3e4adb378ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97361/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "6ee6f458-059f-5089-8b01-9a1e6f548462" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97361/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d741525d-6f40-5084-86dd-75dd3f0c4421" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97361/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-97361/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-97361/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-97361/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-97361/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-97361/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97361" :question/id #uuid "eb77c4e3-9a2f-52aa-a423-e70fc36097a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-97361" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-2)y(-2)+x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=1-2t$ and $q(t)=2-k{t}^{2}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-2)q(-2)+p(0)q(0)+p(2)q(2) \\\\  & =(1+4)(2-4k)+(1)(2)+(1-4)(2-4k) \\\\  & =(10-20k)+2+(-6+12k) \\\\  & =6-8k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6-8k & =0 \\\\ 8k & =6 \\\\ k & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97361/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a348cfec-2c8f-5302-a94a-43a6c9330c34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97361"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-97359"] :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1).\n$$\n\nIf $p(t)=k{t}^{2}-2t$ and $q(t)=2t+1$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(1)q(1)+p(0)q(0)+p(-1)q(-1) \\\\  & =(k-2)(2+1)+(0)(0+1)+(k+2)(-2+1) \\\\  & =(3k-6)+0+(-k-2) \\\\  & =2k-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2k-8 & =0 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140267/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "e219778a-7eb5-5706-8b26-9e32b4c02309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140267/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" :answer/id #uuid "8cd25c22-538c-5602-b649-0696bcae870d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140267/selection/2ec206db7d9c5957ca3e5fc5274fc3c46dd588aa9c1fec980f3093334cfb8725" :answer/id #uuid "61579f7a-6f95-50ba-9f99-7cf5a13bbf47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140267/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "9706f452-8790-5db5-a1c8-f595acc5e682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140267/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb" :answer/id #uuid "48e7f959-822b-58b1-a5e9-8b80dd475353" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140267/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e8e4176-fb66-5003-96d9-81183258db00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140267/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-140267/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-140267/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" "q-140267/selection/2ec206db7d9c5957ca3e5fc5274fc3c46dd588aa9c1fec980f3093334cfb8725" "q-140267/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-140267/selection/ace37c2040207cebb14b55c05840a4c383db24d63f2349cf49f8db6a85f5faeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140267" :question/id #uuid "d512d010-6725-5b0e-a4aa-10b8b5ae97d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-140267" :question/problem "Let $V=C[1,e]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[1,e],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{1}^{e}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIf $x(t)={ln}^{2}⁡(t)+k$ and $y(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}({ln}^{2}⁡(t)+k)\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡(t)}{t}+\\frac{k}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{ln}^{3}⁡(t)}{3}+k\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}+k & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140267/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "404853dd-2cdf-5ee0-b081-ebd6b8a90ee7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140267"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-44069/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "916431d2-23b0-57f5-a625-d6cb0f586704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44069/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" :answer/id #uuid "ca9ba546-f3a6-51cc-8737-8f3f19617c4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44069/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "6f5a308b-352f-5159-af84-b7b395c6e06d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44069/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "910c263f-ff2f-5af8-8446-b51f85c293f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44069/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "74cccbf1-6dd3-5501-ac01-a7f9096ec3e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44069/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff52fd6b-249e-5add-9a46-53ec218a998e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-44069/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer-field/choices ["q-44069/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-44069/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" "q-44069/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-44069/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-44069/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-44069" :question/id #uuid "c3ac8baa-3ca8-5d1d-a2e1-b87529351ba8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44069" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1]\\,,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIf $x(t)=k-2{t}^{3}$ and $y(t)=t$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product is equal to zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}t(k-2{t}^{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(kt-2{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{k{t}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{2{t}^{5}}{5}){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\frac{k}{2}-\\frac{2}{5} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{k}{2} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ k & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-44069/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "404853dd-2cdf-5ee0-b081-ebd6b8a90ee7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-44069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97440/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ac4d7335-3ff1-55ee-988f-ecf05889acab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97440/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "cf6fafbc-3524-5f64-b459-3698df8b35ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value 